00:00:01.240 --> 00:00:04.700
BETH: Individuals with autism
have different cognitive strengths

00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:08.879
and weaknesses but some find
organising, sequencing and

00:00:08.879 --> 00:00:11.040
prioritising really difficult.

00:00:11.620 --> 00:00:15.629
They may have deficits in cognitive
function, which is the intellectual

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:21.490
process by which a person thinks, reasons,
understands ideas and remembers things.

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:25.530
JOE: A person with autism may have
problems with processing information,

00:00:25.950 --> 00:00:29.650
understanding the consequences of their
actions, understanding the concept of

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:34.799
time, or may be detailed focused and
less able to see the whole picture.

00:00:35.519 --> 00:00:39.040
This can affect their ability to
organise, prioritise and sequence.

00:00:39.490 --> 00:00:43.340
BETH: If a person is not able to
understand the concept of time, how

00:00:43.340 --> 00:00:47.519
can they plan what they need to do
over a day, a week, a month or a year.

00:00:48.009 --> 00:00:51.449
This can cause problems in
daily life but can be especially

00:00:51.450 --> 00:00:53.720
difficult in education and work.

00:00:54.340 --> 00:00:58.600
Problems with time perception can make
life more difficult generally, as it

00:00:58.600 --> 00:01:02.330
is an essential part of the way people
make sense of the world around them.

00:01:03.130 --> 00:01:06.740
JOE: Problems with time perception can
also cause delayed reaction to certain

00:01:06.740 --> 00:01:11.529
stimuli, such as speech and this can
present communication problems such as

00:01:11.529 --> 00:01:15.850
not replying to questions or requests,
or saying things later out of context.

00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:21.259
Everyday life for an individual with
autism needs strict routines giving

00:01:21.260 --> 00:01:23.030
them time to process information.

00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:27.520
They need to be helped to develop
strategies to manage their time and

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:31.210
therefore organise their personal
and education and work routines.

00:01:31.210 --> 00:01:31.217
BETH: Let’s now hear from someone about
problems with processing information and

00:01:31.217 --> 00:01:31.239
how it can affect an individual’s life.

